Z||000000||GT Bastard||11-09-1999||07:41 PM||||Allllllright, I was cruizing down a near-empty four lane street here in Sioux Falls, when some Krusy old guy with hockey-hair pulls up next to me in an 80's Thunderbird and floors it.  By the sound of it, the car was a V8, but it had obviously seen better days."  I was going about 40mph, and he was pulling away from me pretty steadily, so I decided to hit the gas... Bye bye, Birdy.  The dude looked pi$$ed off, and I could hear his engine still screaming as I pulled past him.  Of course, after I let off the gas he went screaming by me like an idiot.  I can't say I'm particularly proud of that kill since my opponent was basically driving a Sh!tbox, but at least it was a V8!  Oh yeah, and on the way home some kid in a Ford Taurus wagon tried to race me and lost!!  Big surprise.  We didn't really RACE, but we just kindof of goofed around.  HE started it!<BR>later, kiddies...||||reg||14
Z||000001||Eric||11-09-1999||07:57 PM||||I've lost the feeling of road superiority lately.  I've had to drive my dad's four cylinder Ranger since I've had my engine out.  I'm sure if I ever came across a Fiero, I wouldn't have time enough to read the license plate before the car roared away from me.  That thing is so damn slow.||||reg||1
