Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||11-10-1999||03:17 PM||||I like loud music too. but not distorted music.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyone can crank up the volume on their stereo, but if it's a crappy stereo (as many stock ones are..) then it's all distorted and just sounds bad.<P>I think slapping a few car audio stickers on a ricemobile (amongst all the other stickers asdvertising their performance parts..) and cranking the stock unit up until it's so distorted you can't tell what kind of music they're listening to is pretty dumb.. but I've seen it a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000013||deceler8||11-10-1999||04:10 PM||||Hey, I like loud music too, just not what the riceboys listen to. And that's not limited to just the riceboys...absolutely hilarious to see plain white teenagers listening to the "boom-boom-chit" stuff coming out of their stickered-up Cavaliers.<P>Funniest thing I heard recently was what sounded like polka music blaring out of an import truck (real piece of crap with all the stickers and loud exhaust).<P>This guy must have had 500 watts pumping that stuff...sounded like being at a really cheesy carnival.<P>Alright, no death threats from the polka/gangsta/boom-boom-chit crowd.<P>And I think you know what I mean from my earlier post...this riceburner sounded like someone had taken a $5 transistor radio, turned the volume all the way up, and put it in front of a bullhorn.||||reg||10
